WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:07.229
There are new reports that Donald Trump is
regularly not coming into work until noon

00:00:07.229 --> 00:00:13.460
and that he is rage watching five to seven
Houser's of television every morning.

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:15.650
And my feelings about this are sort of mixed.

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:22.040
Then I'll tell you, why do we want Trump doing
more work in the sense that when Trump works,

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:27.940
he's mostly doing bad things, he's incompetent,
he's hurting people, he's hurting the country

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:29.800
the more that he works.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:30.940
We'll discuss that in a moment.

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:36.760
The report is that Katie Rogers and Annie
CARNEY say at The New York Times that during

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:41.059
coronavirus, Trump has this routine that he's
sort of gotten into, that he's often showing

00:00:41.059 --> 00:00:43.780
up to the Oval Office around noon or later.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:46.370
He's typically in a terrible mood from all
of the TV.

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:47.479
He's been watching all morning.

00:00:47.479 --> 00:00:50.690
It starts as early as 5:00 a.m. with Fox News.

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:51.850
He watches CNN.

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:53.219
He's watching MSNBC.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:59.079
We know this is true because he often tweets
about CNN or about Morning Joe on MSNBC.

00:00:59.079 --> 00:01:00.940
At exactly those times.

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:02.710
And it seems to fire him up even more.

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:05.510
And he's showing up to work very, very upset.

00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:10.079
Trump will also, as he's watching TV for five
to seven hours every morning, he'll get on

00:01:10.079 --> 00:01:15.180
the phone with advisers and complain to them
about how he's not being portrayed as a great

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:17.829
savior when it comes to Corona virus.

00:01:17.829 --> 00:01:22.890
And what we have also learned from this article
in The New York Times excellent article is

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:27.829
that the nightly press briefings that Trump
has been doing most evenings are basically

00:01:27.829 --> 00:01:29.840
the only thing he has to look forward to.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:36.539
And that actually explains a lot and sheds
a ton of light onto the question of we've

00:01:36.539 --> 00:01:41.740
been wondering why is he doing these press
briefings almost constantly.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:46.830
Every single one sees him digging himself
into a deeper and deeper hole, culminating

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:51.409
Thursday with wondering aloud about injecting
bleach and isopropyl alcohol.

00:01:51.409 --> 00:01:52.810
He's not helping himself.

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:54.990
He's arguably hurting himself.

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:59.590
And indeed, it seems as though the reason
he's doing it is because it's all that he

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:00.590
has going on.

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:04.369
And indeed, when you look at Donald Trump's
calendar, it matches up with this reporting.

00:02:04.369 --> 00:02:10.510
Yesterday, for example, Donald Trump's first
scheduled thing was 2 p.m. and it was just

00:02:10.510 --> 00:02:13.130
a conference call last Friday.

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:17.800
Similarly, Trump had nothing on his calendar
before noon when he signed the bill.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:23.250
And then you have his defenders, like, for
example, the new press secretary, Kaley McKenney.

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:29.190
She pops up and she defends Trump and says
it's all fake news and they always go too

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:30.570
far in the defenses.

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:35.840
Like if she put out there a sort of realistic
defense of Trump's work ethic and schedule,

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:37.270
it might be believable.

00:02:37.270 --> 00:02:39.190
But she goes way too far here.

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:43.710
She says Trump is working so much that he
sometimes forgets to eat.

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:48.120
Mark Meadows was asked about what his concern
is day to day as he looks at the president's

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:49.120
schedule.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.970
And he made the point that the president is
so busy and so hard at work.

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:55.050
I mean, his concern is making sure he gets
a bite to eat here and there.

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:57.300
So, you know, you've got to put that into
context.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:00.440
First of all, of course, we are concerned
for America's workers.

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:02.260
So obviously, we know that's not true.

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:04.230
Obviously, Donald Trump is not forgetting
to eat.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:06.830
He is likely technically obese.

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:11.770
If we evaluate what we believe his actual
weight is, there's no indication, whatever,

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:16.490
that he's missing meals unless he is actually
on uppers, as some people suspect.

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:19.340
And uppers tend to take away your appetite.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:23.310
But usually you're making up for it by bingeing
later in the day, once you've come down from

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:24.310
the uppers.

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:25.910
So it just it's not it's too much.

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:26.910
It's not believable.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:32.100
The report that Trump isn't coming until noon
and barely working seems to be well sourced

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:35.830
to then come back and say Trump works harder
than anyone and is sometimes forgetting to

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:36.830
eat.

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:38.690
It's too much and it's not believable.

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:43.450
And that gets us to the practical question
do we want Trump working?

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:47.780
This was a question before the Corona virus
fiasco, before the Corona virus pandemic,

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:49.900
where we would talk about Trump's golf trips.

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:51.280
Trump to date has golf.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:54.340
Two hundred and sixty four days during his
presidency.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:58.080
And that is a sign of an incredibly lazy person
with a poor work ethic.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:05.640
But at the same time, do we want Trump working
when he does terrible things when he actually

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:06.640
works?

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:09.540
We talked about testing earlier today.

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:13.340
Trump should have built a proper testing apparatus
for Corona virus.

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:17.190
He should have built a proper contact tracing
apparatus for Corona virus.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:21.040
But would he have gotten it done if he came
into work at 10 a.m. instead of noon?

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:23.510
Or would he simply have done other things
that would have been bad?

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:24.510
I don't know.

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:29.100
What I can tell you is I've never watched
seven hours of TV in a day in my life.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:35.210
Maybe if I was like home sick, I watched five
hours, maybe like a couple times in my life.

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:36.880
I can't remember this guy.

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:42.280
Is the president and he has time for five
to seven hours of television a day.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:45.060
He often tweets dozens of times a day.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:49.320
He's sometimes gotten close to 100 hundred
tweets and retweets in a single day.

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:53.720
I just run a little independent show with
a few employees and I don't nearly have the

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:54.720
time for this.

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:55.720
This guy's the president.

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:57.190
So it's bizarre.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:59.200
But I want to hear your reaction.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:05.250
Do we really want Trump working more, given
that the more he does, the more bad things

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:06.250
he's doing?

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:07.250
Let me know what you think.

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:26.870
I'm on Twitter

00:05:26.870 --> 00:06:06.639
at

00:06:06.639 --> 00:06:14.810
David Pakman.

